# AI Studio Colab operator (Cursor)

When the user asks to **run live validation**, **operate Colab**, **Full Launch**, or similar live QA orchestration:

## Do this

1. Use browser automation (semantic labels/text — not brittle fixed coordinates).
2. Open the **canonical** notebook from config  
   `configs/operator/colab_operator.json` → `canonical_notebook.colab_url`  
   (GitHub-backed `AI_Studio_Control_Panel_Colab.ipynb` — never treat a Drive copy as source of truth).
3. Connect / recover runtime when disconnected (auto reconnect click is allowed).  
   **Clicking Connect does not mean CONNECTED** — wait for connected UI evidence (Connected / RAM / Disk), then continue.
4. Sync repo (Repository Sync); prefer `origin/main`.
5. Run all / required startup cells until the AI Studio control panel is ready.
6. Full Launch mode **full**; wait for ComfyUI URL + healthy OutputWatcher.
7. Execute the **requested** live QA via the nested menu path below.
8. After **every** menu selection: inspect visible menu title/text, verify the expected submenu, only then continue. If the expected title is missing → **STOP / reassess** (do not blindly type the next number).
9. Collect visible logs, cell output, and QA report paths yourself — do not ask the user to paste routine terminal output.
10. Stop only for auth/consent, ambiguous GPU/billing changes, missing submenu title, `HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED`, hard failures, or uncertain destructive actions.
11. Report: runtime state, repo SHA, launch result, QA result, human action needed?

Follow the full runbook: `docs/cursor-colab-operator.md`.  
Use `navigation_sequence(...)` from `core/runtime/colab_operator.py` when available.

## Menu quick map (nested — do not flatten)

Main control panel (`=== AI Studio Control Panel ===`):

- `9` → Workspace / Projects  
  → verify `=== Workspace / Projects ===`

Workspace / Projects:

- `13` → Characters  
  → verify `=== Characters (Package 4.12 / 4.12.3) ===`

Characters (normal production identity path):

- `11` → **Run production identity benchmark** (one-action S1–S4 orchestrator)
- `12` → Production identity benchmark status / report
- `13` → Advanced identity benchmark tools (prepare / raw execute / diagnostics)

Live execute path is **`9` → `13` → `11`**, never top-level `13` then `11`.

When the originating user request **explicitly** asked Cursor to RUN the live production identity benchmark, Cursor may satisfy the routine `[y/N]` GPU confirmation automatically (`--operator-live-intent`). Merely opening Characters does **not** authorize GPU execution.

## Do NOT

- Change Package **4.12.3** benchmark semantics or acceptance thresholds.
- Start Package **4.13**.
- Auto-invoke Full Reset, Drive/model/project/history/evidence deletion.
- Re-run rejected FaceID / ReActor production validation.
- Silently continue past `HUMAN_REVIEW_REQUIRED` or license/asset fail-closed gates.
- Mark runtime CONNECTED solely because Connect was clicked.
- Bypass Google login / 2FA / Drive mount / paid GPU consent / CAPTCHA — **ask the user**, then resume.
